        "content": "Documents give different answers about the same thing. Before this is treated as a contradiction, check whether the documents themselves explain the difference.\n\nQuestion: What is the profession of S. John Ross?\n\nAnswer A: silhouette artist\n  about: S. John Ross\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"Ross Eastgate, a military historian and journalist, said of Ross that \"He was not tall in stature, but he was giant in Australian entertainment.\"\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: American\n  about: S. John Ross\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"John D. Ross American , born 1946 Indianapolis , IN\" [document 2]\n\nAnswer C: contributor\n  about: S. John Ross\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"\"Risus 1.5\" was named Best Free RPG at RPGnet in 2001 and he contributed to \"Pulp Hero\" which received a Silver ENnie for Best Writing in 2006.\" [document 3]\n\nDocuments:\nDocument 1: knew what the \"S\" in his name stood for. He was sometimes referred to as Scissors John. Ross Eastgate, a military historian and journalist, said of Ross that \"He was not tall in stature, but he was giant in Australian entertainment.\" S. John Ross was born Sebastian John Ross, in Detroit, USA, April 24, 1919. Inspired by an artist that he saw at Michigan State Fair, he trained with the silhouette artist Budd-Jack, travelling around to different fairs for three years. He later worked in Hollywood. During World War II, he served in the Philippines, before a period in Australia\nDocument 2: it began , he ’ s here , covered in sawdust , finding humanity in gnarled wood , baking 12-foot plaster birthday cakes for everyone , casting his brooms in resin and bronze , building robots and writing code . John D. Ross American , born 1946 Indianapolis , IN Indiana State University , B.A . English , 1972 Herron School of Art , Indiana University , B.A . Sculpture , 1992 Select Exhibitions SaatchiArt.com Featured Artist May 25 , 2020 Indianapolis Museum of Art Hoosier Salon Indianapolis , IN . Water Tower Museum Louisville , KY. South Bend Regional\nDocument 3: Award for a short stint as editor of \"Pyramid\" magazine, and was named to the Order of the Pineapple along with author Adam Gorightly in 2013. \"Risus 1.5\" was named Best Free RPG at RPGnet in 2001 and he contributed to \"Pulp Hero\" which received a Silver ENnie for Best Writing in 2006. Ross has been a named guest at several conventions including Technicon in 1995, 1997, and 1998; A-Kon in 2004 and 2009; and Starland Gamefest in 2013. Ross was a special guest at GameFest held in May 2014. S. John Ross was born as Samuel John Ross Jr.,\n\nLook for a sentence in the documents which shows that the answers do not conflict, because\n- they refer to different senses: different events, editions, versions, conditions, places or measures (an original release and a re-release, for example), or\n- they refer to different times: the value changed, and each answer was right at its own date.\nUse only what the documents say: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no explanation of your own. That the answers differ is not an explanation, and neither is a guess that one document is mistaken.\n\nReply with JSON only. If a sentence explains the difference:\n{\"explained\": true, \"by\": \"sense\", \"document\": 1, \"quote\": \"\", \"labels\": {\"A\": \"\", \"B\": \"\"}}\n\"by\" is \"sense\" or \"time\". \"quote\" is that sentence, copied word for word, and \"document\" is the number of the document it is in. \"labels\" gives, for each answer, the sense or the date it refers to.\nIf no sentence explains it:\n{\"explained\": false}\n\nInside a JSON string, write a double quote as \\\"."
